    parentName: "p"
  }, "In the LLM's words, what is this paper about?")), mdx("p", null, "This paper, presented at the 4th Workshop on Natural Language Processing for Indigenous Languages of the Americas (AmericasNLP 2024), focuses on using OCR (Optical Character Recognition)-driven document digitization to preserve and make accessible knowledge in Peruvian Indigenous Languages. The authors propose a method to convert physical documents (e.g., manuscripts, books) into digital text, which can then be used for language revitalization, academic research, and cultural preservation. The work addresses challenges in digitizing languages that are endangered, by leveraging OCR to unlock linguistic resources previously locked in physical form. The project emphasizes practical applications for communities and researchers working with Peruvian Indigenous Languages."), mdx("p", null, "(Note: The paper was published in 2024, though the current date is December 3, 2025\u2014this indicates it was presented at the AmericasNLP 2024 workshop held earlier in 2024.)"), mdx("h5", {
