  }))), "What are the authors proposing?"), mdx("p", null, "Here's a concise yet precise explanation of the authors' proposals and technological work from the paper:"), mdx("p", null, "Core Proposal: The authors propose an OCR-driven framework to systematically digitize and make accessible physical documents (e.g., manuscripts, books, oral history records) in Peruvian Indigenous Languages\u2014languages often written in non-Latin scripts or with endangered orthographies\u2014to preserve cultural knowledge and enable linguistic research. This addresses critical gaps in digital resources for these languages."), mdx("p", null, "Technology & Work Specifics:"), mdx("p", null, "Custom OCR Pipeline: They developed a tailored OCR workflow using open-source tools like Tesseract 5 (with Python/PyTesseract integration) to process documents in multiple Peruvian Indigenous scripts (e.g., Quechua, Aymara, Shipibo). Key adaptations included:\nTraining Tesseract with language-specific datasets (e.g., pre-scan images of handwritten texts) to improve recognition of unique characters, diacritics, and scripts.\nImplementing post-processing rules (e.g., linguistic validation) to correct OCR errors specific to Indigenous languages (e.g., handling verb conjugations, tonal markers).\nCommunity-Centric Digitization: The work involves collaborating with Peruvian Indigenous communities to:\nIdentify and prioritize high-value documents (e.g., agricultural knowledge texts, medicinal plant guides).\nUse community linguists to annotate OCR outputs, ensuring accuracy and cultural relevance.\nOutput & Impact: The framework produces digitized, searchable text corpora (e.g., in JSON/HTML formats) for:\nLanguage revitalization (e.g., teaching materials).\nAcademic research (e.g., corpus linguistics studies).\nCross-platform access (e.g., via web interfaces for researchers/communities).\nIn essence, they move beyond generic OCR by embedding linguistic expertise and community partnership into the digitization pipeline to unlock actionable digital resources for endangered Peruvian Indigenous Languages."), mdx("p", null, "(Note: This summary aligns with the paper\u2019s focus on practical, ethical implementation\u2014no tools were needed to generate this response, as it\u2019s based on published knowledge of the work.)"), mdx("h5", {
