    parentName: "p"
  }, "Describe your process for using the LLM.  How did the LLM perform?")), mdx("p", null, "So I did two versions of this. The first one I didn't make concise, as the rubric said, so I ended up redoing it. I want to share a bit about my first round.\nFirstly, I just told it to tell me about this article, and I sent a link. It ended up summarizing a completely different article, which is when I realized that the base URL I copied could refer to other articles. That was when I exactly mentioned the name and authors of the article, and it got on track... sort of.\nThe first time around, I just asked the assignment questions almost verbatim, and it didn't do so well!\nOkay, onto the time when I mentioned the article's name and authors."), mdx("p", null, "Its responses were thorough and well structured (gotta say, I love organizing things with emojis), and it provided good summaries (in terms of what it generated, not the actual text) in tables and bullet points.\nI had to be pretty specific with questions after what I learned the first time. For example, I specifically asked it to name the two specific OCR software used instead of just 'what approaches' because the first time it rambled on about other stuff - here it gave me two things, the first Tesseract, which was correct, but then Adobe's OCR, which was wrong, the other method it discussed was Google Vision OCR. When I challenged it later on, it said the article never mentioned Google Vision OCR, which is false."), mdx("h4", {
